  "summary_en": "WHO guidance (2021) by an expert group on the ethics and governance of AI in health. It sets out six consensus principles and analyses ethical challenges, liability regimes and governance frameworks for data, the private and public sectors, and regulation. It is almost entirely about software AI, with only passing mentions of robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Six core principles: protect autonomy; promote well-being, safety and public interest; transparency and explainability; responsibility and accountability; inclusiveness and equity; responsive and sustainable AI.",
   "Humans should remain in control of health-care systems and medical decisions.",
   "Calls for regulatory oversight of the private sector, impact assessment and regulatory sandboxes.",
   "Examines liability for AI in clinical care and compensation for harm.",
   "Recommends governance of health data, benefit-sharing and global AI governance, with considerations for LMICs."
